From 1e5a517e46539a199af17466cfcae27538fb6f2e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Vincenzo Ceccarelli Grimaldi <vince.ceccarelli@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 30 Aug 2026 19:58:07 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(v9): case size optimizer + verified reference cluster
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The case-size decision is made once and paid for on every pallet after,
which makes it the expensive question in this niche and the one no free
tool answers well. This adds it, plus the reference pages that carry the
evergreen queries feeding both calculators.

- lib/rectpack.ts: maxCountIn() count-only fast path — verified to agree
  with the full solver on 1,728 shapes with zero mismatches, sweeping
  ~1,500 footprints in 6 ms so a full dimension sweep runs client-side
- lib/caseoptimizer.ts: sweeps every orderable case size, ranks by cube
  utilisation (not cases per pallet, which would reward shipping less),
  collapses rotated duplicates, orients survivors to match the current
  case, and breaks ties toward the least disruptive change
- /tools/case-size-optimizer (en + de): candidate table with the delta in
  percentage points against the user's own case, CSV export
- /reference/pallet-sizes and /reference/container-dimensions (en + de):
  EPAL and ISO figures read off primary sources and cited on the page;
  unpublished values left blank rather than estimated
- Published container pallet counts (20 ft = 11, 40 ft = 25) are asserted
  on the page to come from this site's solver, and a test confirms they do

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
